<div mt-section-origin="Bookshelves/General_Chemistry/Chem1_(Lower)/04:_The_Basics_of_Chemistry/4.05:_Introduction_to_Chemical_Nomenclature" class="mt-section" id="section_5"><span id="Oxyanions"></span><h3 class="lt-chem-3606 editable">Oxyanions</h3>

<p class="lt-chem-3606">The most common oxygen-containing anions (<dfn>oxyanions</dfn>) have names ending in <em>-ate</em>, but if a variant containing a small number of oxygen atoms exists, it takes the suffix <em>-ite</em>.</p>

